readme = _release_expand(f"# Guide error and mandibular canal proximity — research demo\n\nIdea: choose guide system or planning margin based on each site , guide error and channel uncertainty . Furthermore, clinical nerve injury risk requires independent sensory outcomes. Demon delivers geometric scenarios, reviewable upper bounds and a measuring port. No clinical recommendation.\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\ncd @DENTAL_IMPLEMENTATIONS@/X8\n./run_all.sh\n```\n\nPython 3 with system NumPy/SciPy/Matplotlib. The script sets `PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1` to avoid the observed conflict between NumPy2 and Matplotlib compiled for NumPy1. Existing local ToothFairy2 / NV1 - and K3 - inputs are used. R5 re-uses hashbound distance certificates; only remove its own `R5_FULL_GEOMETRY.jsonl` on the data disk for a full conversion. Frozen predictions are never overwritten with changed numeric values .\n\n## Results\n\n{table}\nThe 1 % target applies to **geometric proximity below 1 mm**, not nerve damage. The scenario assumes gamma distributed apex magnitude, isotropic direction, local plane channel boundary and a normal distributed image edge deviation. Moment bound requires valid population elements and an actual anatomic edge budget B=0,3 mm ; these conditions are **not validated**. The figures above are therefore research hypotheses and conditional bounds .\n\nThe margins are numerical breakpoints where the probability/boundary is 1 %. For strict < 1 %, a distance is strictly greater than the cut-off point; the rounded-off values of the table is not a certificate of tolerance. The unrounded values are available in results.json and the original CSV. The ranking of the guides depends on the tail adoption and population transfer.\n\nThe entire implant body against the duct voxel volume is calculated on **2581 sites in 433 case**. All numeric intervals were closed; maximum width {r5['maximum_bracket_gap_mm']:.3g} mm. **37 sites (1,43%) is below 2 mm** despite the previously nominal passed margin. The frozen gate was 5 %: **FAIL**. The median correction of the old distance is 0,094 mm. No measured anatomical correction or nerve damage frequency follows this.\n\nThe old guide error model gives **6,27°**, compared to Tahmaseb's external **3,5°**: frozen ± 1° - gate **FAIL**. Numerical controls with the same information gives **TIE**. Monte Carlo against the analytical scenario check makes the highest difference {max((x['mc_analytic_max_abs_probability_error'] for x in read('CONTROLS_R2.json')['validation'])):.4f} in probability, within frozen 0,005.\n\n![Forskningsresultat](DEMO_FIGURE.png)\n\n## Reference and what is not holds\n\n[Peña-Cardelles 2025 ](https://doi.org/10.4317/medoral.27125) reports 0/68/53 % for the proposed distance groups. Table 2 simultaneously contains 4/316 events at 1 – 2 mm and 1/14 in Kütüks 0 – 1 mm group. A universal 68 % curve is not compatible with the latter group (source-exposed binomial test p=3,63 · 10⁻⁶). This is a transport and source consistency test, not blind external validation or a new clinical incidence estimate. Selection, imaging method, patients/ implant and follow-up are mixed. **Clinical risk per site : UNKNOWN.**\n\nThe magnitudes of the guide errors are derived from independent clinical measurements: [Varga 2020, published table 4, mandible part](https://doi.org/10.1111/clr.13578), and [Wu 2020 , result/Figure 4 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s40729-020-00272-0). Apex is a three-dimensional distance, not a signed depth error. The depth distribution is **UNKNOWN**. [Khaohoen 2024 , Figures 8 – 10 ](https://doi.org/10.1186/s12903-024-04033-y) verifies the metaanalysis context; its mean KI is never used as an individual SD . The patent's 0,55 / 1,14 mm is an approved design step and is not used as a clinical misallocation.\n\nThe channel's frame deviation comes from GEOM_UNC and is labeled towards half-max, not image against anatomy. N's unbound physical canto safety and blooming restrictions remain. Virtual dental shoulder plans on annotated anatomy are not intended or performed surgical implant placements. No sensory follow-up or guide type is tied to these sites .\n\n## The lab can try\n\n[`phantom_manifold/` ](phantom_manifold/) contains the equalized channel insert and block with lumen, millimetres; the planned implant - STL is available in [`phantom/` ](phantom/). Original voxel-STL is preserved there as well. Their channel/block has each one edge with four connecting triangles. The new SDF →tetraheder surface has **0 incorrect edges, 0 incorrect corner links, 0 orientation errors and 0 degenerate/duplicated triangles**. The topology and distance gates of the R6 pass; injected double facet is rejected.\n\n[`PHANTOM_SCENE.json` ](PHANTOM_SCENE.json) indicates coordinates and source hash. The analytical cylinder distance of the original is **1,975139845 mm** to the voxel channel. The closed levelled surface has a new CAD - distance **{meshgap['lower_mm']:.9f} mm** (intervallbredd {meshgap['gap_mm']:.3g} mm): **{r6['maximum_gap_change_mm']:.5f} mm ** change, within frozen 0,3 mm but with changed 2 mm class. [ `FROZEN_MANIFOLD_PHANTOM_PREDICTIONS.json` ](FROZEN_MANIFOLD_PHANTOM_PREDICTIONS.json) preserves the new prediction separately. Furthermore, the 64 facet STL of the implant differs from the ideal cylinder by a maximum of 0,002410 mm. Compare a manufactured levelled part with its own frozen reference.\n\nManufacturing and independent metrology are not performed. The closed topology of the surface does not certify support, lumen access, material/process or tolerances; these are determined before measurement. Geometry can be used as a channel insert in a test block. No anatomical or clinical validation results from SDF exports.\n\n[Fantom's channel and implant ](PHANTOM_PREVIEW.png)\n\nMeasure `lost margin = planned minimum distance − measured minimum distance + metrology budget` per independent block. [`CALIBRATION_TEMPLATE.csv`](CALIBRATION_TEMPLATE.csv) and [`calibrate_clearance.py`](calibrate_clearance.py) accept these data. [Wilks/NIST tolerance bound](https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/software/dataplot/refman1/auxillar/tolelimi.htm) requires **299 independent blocks** for one fixed guide or **437 per guide** for four candidates, for <1 % tail risk with 95 % family confidence. Published 37 fully guided mandibulary implant is not enough: optimistic iid floor 7,78%; truly independent n is unknown due to patient clustering.\n\n```bash\npython3 calibrate_clearance.py --csv uppmatta_block.csv --x 0.01 --confidence 0.95 --candidates 4 --anatomy-budget-mm 0.3\n```\n\nThe 0,3 budget may be entered in that command only if it is independent for the current application. Calibrated phantom geometry does not validate clinical nerve disorders or transfer to another surgical situation.\n\n## Data, cost and auditability\n\nToothFairy2 : **CC BY-SA 4.0**, source [the organizer's dataset](https://toothfairy2.grand-challenge.org/dataset/), local archive; outputs here is processed annotation geometry. The EuropePMC articles have their respective licenses in the preserved XML; Varga-PDF is the accepted manuscript of the repository, its copyright text preserved. Published aggregates are reproduced as facts. No second patient data sets or personal data are used. K3 archive metadata declares 480 case, but 479 actual case- JSON exists; all 2706 site lines are accurately verified against the frozen input. The missing case identity is UNKNOWN ; the 2581 completed sites in the 433 case are not affected.\n\nFull first geometry conversion: **122,11 s**, a thread, top RSS **349 MiB**, no GPU . Separate source verification reread all 433 labels/plans and checked 54 682 voxelwitnesses: **{read('SOURCE_VERIFICATION.json')['wall_seconds']:.2f} s**, **{read('SOURCE_VERIFICATION.json')['maxrss_kib'] / 1024:.0f} MiB**. Closed SDF phantom with topology and distance review: **{r6['cost']['wall_seconds']:.2f} s**, **{r6['cost']['maxrss_kib'] / 1024:.0f} MiB**. Literature search, code construction and future measurement are not included in these times; human equivalent cost is UNKNOWN. Re-use K3 construction cost previously 2904,30 s ; second predecessor's preparation cost is UNKNOWN . Own data/intermediate is under 0,2 GB , with hash manifest. [ `results.json` ](results.json), six PREREG , raw certificate, frozen predictions and [ `VERIFICATION.json` ](VERIFICATION.json) separates measurement , derivation , model admission, negative gate and UNKNOWN . Injected bugs rejects all critical numerical and calibration checks. [ `MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_PORT.md` ](MINIMUM_MEASUREMENT_PORT.md) specifies the measurement and [ `SOURCE_EXTRACTION.md` ](SOURCE_EXTRACTION.md) source assets. The graph dispatch was stopped by `STALE_INPUT` for X5 : s result, and feedback could therefore not be recorded; the logs are preserved. Status **PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW**.\n")
